PRODUCERS:

02:26.420 --> 02:29.420
YASHIMA TOKUHARA

02:26.420 --> 02:29.420
SATSUKI MIZUNO

02:26.420 --> 02:29.420
YOSHIHIKO FUJISAWA

02:33.670 --> 02:36.670
DIRECTED BY: MAMORU KANBE

02:37.280 --> 02:39.500
This makes eighteen demons.

02:39.500 --> 02:42.310
Damn, they’re all so small these days.

02:42.310 --> 02:43.760
They don’t even fight back.

02:43.760 --> 02:46.840
Remember, our main objective is
not to destroy them.

02:47.620 --> 02:51.340
It should be to capture and send back...

02:51.340 --> 02:54.770
those who’ve escaped
from the Underworld.

02:54.770 --> 02:57.280
Yeah, I know.

02:57.280 --> 02:59.470
Anyway, it’s so hot...

03:11.290 --> 03:16.300
The summer-like heat continues
day after day in late May.

03:16.890 --> 03:22.300
People on the streets are confused over
this unseasonably early heat wave.

03:22.300 --> 03:23.800
This is terrible...

03:23.800 --> 03:27.890
I can’t just go out
if it’s this hot from now.

03:30.890 --> 03:32.680
Phew...

03:33.330 --> 03:36.520
I’m glad I bought this for the summer.

03:36.520 --> 03:37.890
Achoo!

03:37.890 --> 03:40.230
It’s freezing. Turn off the ac Kapaeru!

03:40.230 --> 03:41.710
What?!

03:41.710 --> 03:43.780
If you do that, I’ll turn you into ice!

03:44.130 --> 03:45.700
What have you set it to anyway?

03:45.700 --> 03:47.300
Zero degrees. A bit high, isn’t it?

03:47.300 --> 03:48.080
Kappa!

03:48.080 --> 03:51.530
No, no, you don’t have to
listen to that one.

03:51.530 --> 03:52.930
What do you mean “that one”?

03:52.930 --> 03:54.690
Kappa! You hear me or what!

03:54.690 --> 03:56.630
Wh-Wh-What?

03:57.400 --> 03:58.130
Yes?

03:58.760 --> 04:01.320
Huh? What?

04:01.320 --> 04:04.030
Come on, you two...

04:06.560 --> 04:08.410
Huh? Wait, what, huh?

04:09.350 --> 04:11.270
Sat-chan

04:09.350 --> 04:11.270
To Kapa-chan

04:09.350 --> 04:11.270
I want to meet you.

04:12.080 --> 04:15.440
Sat-chan says she wants to
meet me in person and talk...

04:15.440 --> 04:16.900
Why don’t you meet her?

04:16.900 --> 04:19.780
I can’t meet her looking like this!

04:19.780 --> 04:22.780
Just tell her you’re in a costume,
like you always say.

04:26.140 --> 04:28.940
I sent her a photo before...

04:28.940 --> 04:32.040
To her, that’s me...

04:34.290 --> 04:39.300
BENZAITEN
SHRINE

04:54.490 --> 04:55.190
Hey!

04:55.190 --> 04:56.690
Kapa-chan!

04:56.690 --> 04:58.150
Oh, yeah...

04:58.150 --> 04:59.620
I’m so happy!

04:59.620 --> 05:00.940
You really came!

05:00.940 --> 05:02.820
Well...

05:04.780 --> 05:07.280
He seems to be doing fine.

05:07.280 --> 05:12.600
He was saying, “What am I supposed to
talk to a kid about!” But...

05:12.600 --> 05:14.630
I feel a bit relieved now.

05:14.630 --> 05:17.460
Despite what you may think,
he quite likes children.

05:22.200 --> 05:23.670
Sat-chan...

05:23.670 --> 05:26.680
I’m glad she’s having fun...

05:27.080 --> 05:28.410
...really.

05:30.190 --> 05:36.000
I’m also feeling a little conflicted,
even if he’s with a child like her.

05:37.210 --> 05:38.560
Miss...

05:41.520 --> 05:45.430
Did she wanna see me ’cause
something was troubling her?

05:45.430 --> 05:49.070
Yep, I thought she had
information on demons.

05:49.070 --> 05:50.450
But nothing to worry about.

05:50.450 --> 05:55.230
Her parents are having problems and
they hit her sometimes.

05:55.230 --> 05:56.470
What are you saying?

05:56.470 --> 05:58.240
That’s serious!

05:59.040 --> 06:02.000
And what did you tell her, boss?

06:02.500 --> 06:04.550
Parents or not...

06:04.550 --> 06:06.590
if they hit you, strike back immediately.

06:06.590 --> 06:08.010
I see...

06:10.070 --> 06:16.050
Oh, and she got you a present but
forgot it, so she’ll send it later.

06:16.050 --> 06:17.600
Hm? A present?

06:32.340 --> 06:34.270
Welcome home, Sachiko.

06:35.670 --> 06:38.540
Where were you until this time?

06:42.560 --> 06:44.900
I-I’m sorry,

06:44.900 --> 06:47.010
I just went to see a friend.

06:47.010 --> 06:48.730
I see...

06:49.920 --> 06:53.890
Playing until this late...

06:53.890 --> 06:55.430
you’re a bad girl.

06:55.430 --> 06:57.360
M-Mommy?

06:57.360 --> 07:00.390
Even you’re making a fool out of me?

07:00.390 --> 07:01.190
What?

07:09.030 --> 07:10.400
I’m going to punish you.

07:20.330 --> 07:22.630
TO COMPLETELY SOLVE
ANY SUPERNATURAL OR
MYSTERIOUS INCIDENTS,
ENMA'S DETECTIVE
AGENCY

07:23.080 --> 07:25.240
Inspector! Midori Akaki is!

07:28.760 --> 07:30.250
It’s coming...

07:30.250 --> 07:32.950
It’s coming again...

07:38.270 --> 07:39.640
No!

07:41.220 --> 07:42.820
Don’t come!

07:43.860 --> 07:46.070
It’s... It’s...

07:46.070 --> 07:49.230
It’s awake!

07:49.790 --> 07:51.240
Miss...

07:51.240 --> 07:53.120
Are you okay, Yuki-chan?

07:53.680 --> 07:58.500
She got sick from walking around in the heat.

07:59.200 --> 08:01.270
Kapa-chan, you’ve got mail.

08:05.960 --> 08:07.610
It’s from Sat-chan.

08:08.130 --> 08:09.350
A thanks for today?

08:11.220 --> 08:12.470
Help, will get killed.

08:11.220 --> 08:12.470
Sat-chan

08:12.790 --> 08:16.380
What?! Boss, Sat-chan will get killed!

08:16.380 --> 08:18.000
Killed?

08:18.000 --> 08:19.520
By the parents she talked about today?

08:19.520 --> 08:24.060
’Cause you said that, she may have
really struck back...

08:24.060 --> 08:26.630
Doesn’t mean she’ll be killed.

08:26.630 --> 08:28.890
Anyhow, let’s go check it out!

08:28.890 --> 08:30.830
Damn, what bother.

08:31.500 --> 08:35.950
That girl is sensitive to
suspicious things, isn’t she?

08:36.520 --> 08:38.530
You should go just in case...

08:38.530 --> 08:41.620
Even if you don’t go, I’m going!

08:41.620 --> 08:42.370
Wait.

08:43.110 --> 08:44.800
You stay here, Yuki-chan.

08:44.800 --> 08:46.730
B-Boss!

08:46.730 --> 08:49.380
Well, I don’t think it’s demon related...

08:49.810 --> 08:52.130
but as she did buy me an ice cream...

08:52.130 --> 08:54.180
Don’t overdo it.

08:54.180 --> 08:56.650
Princess, that bruise?

08:56.650 --> 08:58.180
Oh, this?

08:58.180 --> 08:59.950
It appears sometimes.

09:00.500 --> 09:03.140
It doesn’t hurt or anything.

09:04.430 --> 09:05.760
Let’s go, Geezer.

09:11.020 --> 09:13.780
According to the address,
it must be this house.

09:14.430 --> 09:16.690
Just a normal looking house.

09:24.210 --> 09:26.620
Stop! What’s wrong, Mommy?

09:27.120 --> 09:29.240
Didn’t I tell you?

09:29.240 --> 09:31.590
Bad girls get punished.

09:38.850 --> 09:40.600
No!

09:49.450 --> 09:50.820
Don’t come!

09:50.820 --> 09:52.920
Daddy, help me!

09:52.920 --> 09:54.580
Mommy is!

09:56.220 --> 09:58.340
Why do you run away?

09:58.340 --> 10:00.070
No!

10:29.460 --> 10:32.770
No... D-Don’t come...

10:37.390 --> 10:41.400
Mommy punished daddy, too.

10:46.570 --> 10:48.460
No... Stop mommy!

11:02.050 --> 11:04.100
Ouch!

11:04.580 --> 11:06.110
You’re getting ahead of yourself.

11:06.110 --> 11:07.460
Kapa-chan!

11:10.910 --> 11:13.770
This woman is possessed by a demon.

11:15.020 --> 11:15.970
Mommy!

11:15.970 --> 11:17.030
Run away!

11:17.030 --> 11:19.240
Stop it!

11:19.240 --> 11:20.600
Let go!

11:20.600 --> 11:24.120
No! Let go of me!

11:24.120 --> 11:26.410
Be quiet!

11:30.280 --> 11:32.840
This is... This demon is!

12:11.250 --> 12:15.250
Ow! Ouch! Oh no!

12:15.250 --> 12:16.910
I won’t let you escape.

12:16.910 --> 12:19.060
Listen Enma, this demon is...

12:19.060 --> 12:21.710
Talk later, must deal with this now.

12:21.710 --> 12:23.260
No!

12:23.260 --> 12:24.870
Don’t kill her!

12:27.070 --> 12:28.760
Shit, I won’t let you escape.

12:28.760 --> 12:31.520
Mommy! What’s wrong? Mommy!

12:31.520 --> 12:34.100
’Cause the demon who possessed her
has escaped...

12:34.910 --> 12:37.720
your mom should return to normal...

12:38.330 --> 12:39.280
I think...

12:39.280 --> 12:41.610
Wh-Who are you? You two?

12:43.400 --> 12:45.700
I guess that’s it for our E-mails.

12:46.800 --> 12:48.880
Could you be?

12:48.880 --> 12:51.130
Goodbye!

13:01.460 --> 13:02.650
Snow?

13:09.240 --> 13:12.250
Damn, I can’t even feel its presence.

13:12.250 --> 13:15.100
We should have brought along Yuki-chan.

13:15.100 --> 13:22.650
Sat-chan, what is she going to do
with her parents in such a state...

13:22.650 --> 13:25.510
That’s none of our concern.

13:25.510 --> 13:27.030
We’re leaving, Kapaeru!

13:28.530 --> 13:30.780
I’m gonna stay a little to check on...

13:33.260 --> 13:34.530
Do what you want.

13:34.530 --> 13:37.750
Quite troublesome that
we let it escape again.

13:37.750 --> 13:40.420
Huh, wherever it goes I’ll...

13:42.990 --> 13:44.400
Again?

13:44.400 --> 13:47.060
That surge of evil was the same as...

13:47.060 --> 13:51.060
the first demon we destroyed
in the human world.

13:51.060 --> 13:52.440
Don’t talk crap!

13:52.440 --> 13:54.140
That time I’m sure I...

13:59.540 --> 14:04.660
Must be quite a demon
to conspire against us...

14:06.800 --> 14:09.720
It doesn’t sit well with me...

14:09.720 --> 14:12.950
Where has it been hiding all this time?

14:40.850 --> 14:40.900
Delete
Sat-chan?

14:44.860 --> 14:44.900
Sat-chan
deleted.

14:47.860 --> 14:49.070
MAY   21   (FRI)

14:47.860 --> 14:49.070
EMAIL     MENU     MY SELECT

14:49.390 --> 14:50.550
Anyway...

14:51.910 --> 14:53.580
it would have ended like this someday.

14:55.330 --> 14:56.540
Sa-Sat-chan.

14:57.910 --> 14:58.500
Wait!

15:23.970 --> 15:25.930
This is... for me?

15:25.930 --> 15:28.040
I forgot to give it to you.

15:32.930 --> 15:34.150
Sat-chan...

15:36.280 --> 15:38.240
How’s your wound?

15:38.240 --> 15:39.830
Never mind that...

15:39.830 --> 15:41.120
How about you, Sat-chan?

15:42.410 --> 15:44.400
I called the police...

15:45.460 --> 15:50.130
M-Mommy doesn’t move
like she’s asleep...

15:55.410 --> 15:57.510
I’ll help you!

15:57.510 --> 16:00.560
I’ll do whatever I can!

16:00.560 --> 16:01.520
So...

16:02.570 --> 16:04.960
Thanks... Kapa-chan.

16:07.020 --> 16:08.270
Snow?

16:37.440 --> 16:39.690
Sat-chan...

16:50.770 --> 16:54.360
Ki... ku... ko...

17:04.330 --> 17:05.500
Kikuko!

17:22.230 --> 17:23.700
What’s going on?

17:24.280 --> 17:25.820
Stench of a demon.

17:25.820 --> 17:26.770
What?!

17:26.770 --> 17:30.490
I never expected it to come after us...

17:30.490 --> 17:31.520
Yuki-chan?!

17:31.520 --> 17:32.820
Where’s Yuki-chan?

17:39.640 --> 17:42.380
Boss... I got hit.

17:42.380 --> 17:44.990
Kapaeru! What’s wrong? Where’re you?

17:44.990 --> 17:46.350
Miss was...

17:47.610 --> 17:48.840
Yuki-chan?

17:48.840 --> 17:49.710
What happened to Yuki-chan?

17:51.000 --> 17:53.420
So... rry...

17:53.870 --> 17:56.140
Kapaeru! Kapaeru!

17:56.140 --> 17:57.930
You bastard! Answer me!

17:58.360 --> 18:00.440
Hey, Kappa!

18:06.520 --> 18:08.060
Unforgivable!

18:16.050 --> 18:17.280
“Missing?”

18:17.280 --> 18:20.170
“Yes, it’s been five months already.”

18:20.170 --> 18:23.380
“He just suddenly disappeared
into thin air one day...”

18:24.760 --> 18:27.290
“On what day did
Detective Abashiri disappear??”

18:27.290 --> 18:32.790
TO COMPLETELY SOLVE
ANY SUPERNATURAL OR
MYSTERIOUS INCIDENTS,
ENMA'S DETECTIVE
AGENCY

18:28.470 --> 18:32.780
He disappeared the day
Midori Akaki died a strange death.

18:35.300 --> 18:38.750
They said the detective was
heading here...

18:47.820 --> 18:50.190
It seems this is
no ordinary abandoned place.

18:54.950 --> 18:56.990
Wow!

19:12.840 --> 19:14.430
Something smells burnt.

19:15.340 --> 19:17.790
Like something is on fire...

19:57.610 --> 19:58.720
A child?

19:59.250 --> 20:01.050
Maybe this is a play area?

20:07.020 --> 20:09.640
Kiyoshi

20:10.800 --> 20:12.100
This ball...

20:30.480 --> 20:31.840
Anybody there?

20:51.470 --> 20:53.440
Wh-What’s this?

21:21.740 --> 21:25.110
He should change his name to “Perv-naga.”

21:25.110 --> 21:26.970
Or more like “Dork-naga.”

21:25.650 --> 21:28.350
TEACHERS' LOUNGE

21:42.360 --> 21:46.130
Yoshinaga is gross.
He has such a lecherous gaze.

21:46.130 --> 21:48.870
Yeah, he does. Gross.

21:48.870 --> 21:52.370
He should change his name to “Perv-naga.”

21:52.370 --> 21:54.100
Or more like “Dork-naga.”

21:56.410 --> 22:01.880
OUT OF RANGE

21:57.080 --> 21:58.690
I can’t go on...

21:58.690 --> 22:01.880
It won’t be funny if we get lost now.

22:02.250 --> 22:05.260
Daiko! Don’t say such a frightening thing!

22:05.260 --> 22:07.300
Then keep walking.

22:08.150 --> 22:09.370
C’mon.

22:09.370 --> 22:10.430
Okay...

22:19.050 --> 22:19.630
What?

22:19.630 --> 22:20.500
Snow?

22:20.500 --> 22:21.470
What?

22:21.470 --> 22:24.610
It’s too early, even for a mountain, isn’t it?

22:31.740 --> 22:33.020
What is it?

22:33.020 --> 22:34.110
No clue.

22:34.110 --> 22:35.870
Oh, we should ask for directions!

22:35.870 --> 22:38.150
Hello?

22:38.150 --> 22:39.570
Wait for me!

22:44.990 --> 22:46.080
What’s wrong?

22:49.050 --> 22:50.390
Here, in a place like this?

24:06.740 --> 24:07.900
Daiko...

24:07.900 --> 24:09.560
Hello?

24:09.560 --> 24:10.890
Daiko!

24:11.560 --> 24:14.580
But we’ll definitely get lost
if we don’t do anything.

24:30.720 --> 24:31.720
The light went on.

24:32.290 --> 24:36.410
If the light went on,
somebody must be here, right?

24:36.410 --> 24:37.420
I guess...

24:52.960 --> 24:56.500
They must know that we’ve come in, right?

24:56.500 --> 24:57.490
Yep.

25:07.660 --> 25:08.600
Hey...

25:09.290 --> 25:11.660
Isn’t this place a bit suffocating?

25:11.660 --> 25:14.270
Yeah, I thought so, too.

25:14.270 --> 25:16.120
Something is strange.

25:29.280 --> 25:30.840
An examination room?

25:30.840 --> 25:32.410
A hospital?

25:32.410 --> 25:33.440
In a place like this?

25:33.440 --> 25:35.380
How should I know?

25:38.260 --> 25:40.450
That’s strange!

25:40.450 --> 25:43.640
An examination room should
at least have a phone.

26:10.070 --> 26:11.000
What?

26:12.300 --> 26:14.230
Where is this?

26:24.810 --> 26:27.460
Calm down, calm down...

26:27.460 --> 26:28.780
Try to remember.

26:33.960 --> 26:35.830
I was in an abandoned building...

26:37.030 --> 26:38.700
A ball fell...

26:38.700 --> 26:40.030
then...

26:40.030 --> 26:41.400
then...

26:41.400 --> 26:42.920
Don’t move!

26:42.920 --> 26:44.600
Put your hands up!

26:45.980 --> 26:47.040
I knew it!

26:48.270 --> 26:49.670
Why are you here?!

26:50.180 --> 26:51.730
And you too, Detective!

26:52.990 --> 26:56.160
I’ve been searching all over for you.

26:56.160 --> 26:57.580
Searching?

26:57.580 --> 27:00.030
So, where are we?

27:00.030 --> 27:02.590
I was also brought here just now.

27:02.590 --> 27:05.430
Now? Then where have you been until now?

27:05.430 --> 27:06.220
Huh?

27:06.220 --> 27:08.940
Detective, you disappeared in May, right?

27:08.940 --> 27:11.060
Wait! What are you talking about?

27:11.060 --> 27:12.560
It’s October now.

27:12.560 --> 27:13.650
October?!

27:21.250 --> 27:23.470
Does it mean the time skipped?

27:24.230 --> 27:29.670
Unless you’ve been asleep for more than
five months or suddenly lost your memory.

27:29.670 --> 27:31.490
That would seem to be the case.

27:32.030 --> 27:36.260
You and I both went to that place
and were brought here.

27:37.000 --> 27:38.620
That’s the common factor.

27:39.640 --> 27:42.740
Theory can come later.

27:42.740 --> 27:45.180
Getting out of here is a priority.

27:45.180 --> 27:46.940
True enough.

27:50.020 --> 27:51.290
What are you doing?

27:51.290 --> 27:53.610
This is quite a
mysterious phenomenon, isn’t it?

27:54.190 --> 27:56.170
You come to a place like this and
you’re still on your job?

27:56.170 --> 27:56.940
Let me be.

27:58.050 --> 28:00.670
It calms me down if I think like that.

28:04.720 --> 28:05.940
Oh, yeah!

28:05.940 --> 28:07.660
Didn’t you hear that a while ago?

28:07.660 --> 28:09.330
Like a woman’s scream.

28:09.820 --> 28:11.410
A woman’s scream?

28:11.410 --> 28:12.830
From downstairs.

28:16.070 --> 28:19.040
I didn’t mean to frighten you.

28:19.040 --> 28:20.220
Sorry.

28:20.830 --> 28:27.010
I heard your voices
when I was looking around for the resident.

28:27.010 --> 28:30.480
Oh, I’m Yoshinaga, a high school teacher.

28:31.170 --> 28:32.770
I’m Hiroko Hoin.

28:33.390 --> 28:35.390
Everyone calls me Daiko.

28:35.390 --> 28:36.980
I’m Ayu Ayukawa.

28:37.670 --> 28:39.030
Students?

28:39.030 --> 28:40.720
Second year of college.

28:40.720 --> 28:45.080
We were trekking when it started
snowing all of a sudden.

28:46.910 --> 28:48.010
Snow?

28:48.010 --> 28:52.600
That’s right, there was a woman
just like snow, here.

28:52.600 --> 28:54.750
I saw her! That’s why I came here.

28:56.660 --> 28:58.670
The one wearing a white kimono?

28:58.670 --> 29:01.690
With long hair... You saw her, too?

29:02.480 --> 29:05.220
Yes, but we saw her near here.

29:05.220 --> 29:07.390
There is somebody living here, for sure.

29:07.390 --> 29:10.180
First, we have to find that woman.

29:11.270 --> 29:13.120
Just as I thought. Something is strange.

29:13.690 --> 29:14.690
What?

29:14.690 --> 29:16.020
There aren’t any...

29:16.560 --> 29:18.370
There’re no windows here.

29:18.770 --> 29:20.250
That’s it!

29:20.250 --> 29:22.730
I was thinking that
something was not right here.

29:22.730 --> 29:24.280
Why are there no windows?

29:24.280 --> 29:26.110
How should I know?

29:26.110 --> 29:28.320
Hey Daiko, I’m scared.

29:28.320 --> 29:29.800
Let’s leave.

29:29.800 --> 29:31.170
The rain may have stopped.

29:31.170 --> 29:33.010
But, it’s night already.

29:33.010 --> 29:34.560
This is a mountain, right?

29:34.560 --> 29:36.850
It’s wise to wait until the morning.

29:36.850 --> 29:38.810
A mountain path is dangerous at night.

29:40.280 --> 29:43.150
By the way, where did you two come in from?

29:43.720 --> 29:45.400
From where?

29:45.400 --> 29:47.960
The front door as usual.

29:51.810 --> 29:52.610
S-Sir?

29:52.610 --> 29:54.490
Can you take me there?

29:54.490 --> 29:55.300
Huh?

29:55.300 --> 29:58.810
Nevermind, just take me to the place
you entered from.

29:58.810 --> 30:00.440
Oh, okay...

30:02.000 --> 30:03.790
I think we turned there and...

30:03.790 --> 30:05.120
Yep...

30:05.120 --> 30:06.020
see.

30:09.600 --> 30:10.450
It can’t be!

30:10.970 --> 30:12.060
How come?!

30:12.060 --> 30:13.470
Just as I thought.

30:13.470 --> 30:14.330
What?

30:17.010 --> 30:19.680
I tried to get out from here, too...

30:19.680 --> 30:21.960
but the same thing happened to me.

30:21.960 --> 30:25.340
You mean, we’re locked in?

30:25.340 --> 30:29.140
I don’t know what kind of a trick this is,
but yes, we are.

30:29.140 --> 30:29.970
Why?

30:29.970 --> 30:32.640
Who would do such a thing? Why?

30:32.640 --> 30:35.840
Calm down. No point panicking.

30:35.840 --> 30:37.820
We are locked in?!

30:36.410 --> 30:39.000
Look Ayu... Ayu!

30:37.820 --> 30:39.000
What have we done?!

30:39.000 --> 30:40.670
We just came to the mountain!

30:39.000 --> 30:40.670
Ayu, calm down!

30:40.670 --> 30:42.730
I’m calm!

30:46.000 --> 30:48.340
Can’t find anybody.

30:48.340 --> 30:50.010
Nor an exit.

30:50.010 --> 30:51.170
Not even a window.

30:51.170 --> 30:53.020
What do we do now?

30:53.020 --> 30:53.700
Huh?

30:54.200 --> 30:55.500
What?

31:09.140 --> 31:10.110
What’s wrong?

31:42.450 --> 31:44.260
Is there somebody here or not?

31:44.260 --> 31:45.370
Which is it?

31:46.710 --> 31:48.470
Hey, what’s wrong?

31:48.470 --> 31:50.890
What? Did you say something?

31:50.890 --> 31:52.210
What’s wrong with the painting?

31:52.210 --> 31:53.200
Painting?

31:53.200 --> 31:54.510
You were staring at it.

31:54.510 --> 31:56.150
Oh, really?

31:56.710 --> 31:57.940
Anyway...

32:10.110 --> 32:11.900
W-Wait!

32:11.900 --> 32:14.060
We haven’t done...

32:14.060 --> 32:15.820
Where did you guys come from?

32:15.820 --> 32:16.650
What?

32:18.550 --> 32:20.440
Metropolitan Police,
Criminal Investigations 1st Division.

32:20.440 --> 32:22.170
Naojiro Abashiri.

32:22.170 --> 32:24.070
You’re a police officer?

32:26.350 --> 32:30.510
Miss Hoin and Miss Ayukawa,
you stumbled upon this building...

32:30.510 --> 32:32.740
when you almost got lost in the mountain.

32:33.800 --> 32:36.410
Mr. Yoshinaga, you were here
when you came to.

32:37.200 --> 32:39.610
Though the time is different...

32:39.610 --> 32:44.200
we both lost consciousness
in Kagurazaka and came here.

32:44.200 --> 32:45.790
Is this everyone?

32:45.790 --> 32:47.190
Why do you say that?

32:47.540 --> 32:49.520
I feel like someone’s watching us.

32:50.080 --> 32:53.820
Ever since arriving in this unknown place.

32:53.820 --> 32:57.880
That must be that woman in the white kimono.

32:57.880 --> 33:00.390
And she is watching us...

33:07.600 --> 33:08.550
For me?

33:11.290 --> 33:13.460
I couldn’t use it before...

33:15.660 --> 33:17.880
Mine still doesn’t work...

33:17.880 --> 33:19.610
Mine, either.

33:18.430 --> 33:21.440
You've got mail
from Mr.Sosuke.

33:18.430 --> 33:21.440
EMAIL

33:19.610 --> 33:21.430
What company is yours?

33:26.330 --> 33:28.310
You did it.

33:31.250 --> 33:32.260
Daiko?

33:32.900 --> 33:35.750
A direct mail. It’s out of range now...

33:35.750 --> 33:38.330
Probably just a random electrical wave.

33:38.330 --> 33:39.290
I see...

33:39.290 --> 33:41.950
Well, it doesn’t seem to be abandoned...

33:41.950 --> 33:44.540
if the resident is out,
we’ll just wait until the morning.

33:44.540 --> 33:47.630
Should you be making
such a lighthearted comment?

33:48.340 --> 33:49.880
You should know!

33:51.160 --> 33:53.060
This place is strange.

33:53.060 --> 33:56.880
Maybe we can never get out of here...

33:56.880 --> 33:58.610
That can’t be!

33:58.610 --> 34:01.130
There must be an exit somewhere!

34:01.890 --> 34:03.030
There must be.

34:07.280 --> 34:08.600
Can’t you hear that?

34:17.390 --> 34:19.620
Träumerei...

35:28.180 --> 35:28.980
It’s here...

35:36.030 --> 35:37.150
A piano?

35:37.770 --> 35:39.650
There’s nobody here.

35:39.650 --> 35:41.640
But it was this room, right?

35:41.640 --> 35:44.280
Hey, who was playing?

35:44.930 --> 35:48.160
There was sound right up to
when we entered.

35:52.420 --> 35:54.040
There are four exits but...

35:54.660 --> 35:57.550
nobody heard anybody leaving, right?

35:59.440 --> 36:01.760
No... No more.

36:02.070 --> 36:04.250
I don’t want any more! Let’s leave!

36:04.250 --> 36:09.770
No! Let’s get out of this room now!

36:04.570 --> 36:06.350
It’s okay Ayu.

36:06.350 --> 36:08.910
I’ll protect you no matter what.

36:08.910 --> 36:09.770
Ayu!

36:12.100 --> 36:13.770
What a face you had.

36:15.980 --> 36:17.860
I’ll check out the rest.

36:17.860 --> 36:19.710
You guys go back to that room.

36:19.710 --> 36:20.800
I’m coming, too.

36:20.800 --> 36:22.640
It’s dangerous for a woman.

36:23.300 --> 36:25.010
I’ll go, too.

36:25.010 --> 36:27.070
Oh, thanks.

36:27.070 --> 36:28.700
Women return to the room, okay?

36:28.700 --> 36:30.580
Damn!

36:43.990 --> 36:47.890
I’m glad the men with us
are a policeman and a teacher.

36:48.280 --> 36:49.340
If they were weird...

36:49.340 --> 36:52.640
Police or teacher, it’s just a job.

36:52.640 --> 36:53.430
What?

36:53.430 --> 36:56.830
I mean a title is nothing here.

36:56.830 --> 36:58.700
Don’t let your guard down.

36:59.210 --> 37:01.070
I wonder which this is?

37:01.070 --> 37:02.360
Huh? What?

37:02.360 --> 37:04.470
The person in this painting.

37:05.220 --> 37:07.120
There are six.

37:07.120 --> 37:10.780
I can see three women and two men...

37:10.780 --> 37:13.090
but is the last one a man?

37:13.090 --> 37:14.710
Or a woman?

37:16.140 --> 37:17.500
I don’t know...

37:20.070 --> 37:22.160
Are you a detective?

37:22.160 --> 37:22.880
Yeah.

37:22.880 --> 37:25.450
What do you think of all this?

37:26.440 --> 37:28.140
There must be somebody else.

37:28.140 --> 37:30.770
And probably, that’s the one who...

37:34.140 --> 37:35.700
I’m thirsty.

37:35.700 --> 37:37.110
The water bottle?

37:37.110 --> 37:38.330
It’s already empty.

37:38.330 --> 37:39.330
No way!

37:42.900 --> 37:44.450
That’s not good.

37:44.450 --> 37:46.340
We can’t last without water.

37:46.340 --> 37:48.610
There must be at least a tap somewhere.

37:48.610 --> 37:52.760
No! Detective told us not to leave.

37:52.760 --> 37:53.960
Wait until they return.

37:53.960 --> 37:56.060
Just gonna look around the corner.

38:01.230 --> 38:02.910
I’ll return immediately, if there’s nothing.

38:02.910 --> 38:04.230
I’m going, too!

38:06.240 --> 38:07.790
You stay behind.

38:07.790 --> 38:09.430
I don’t want to be away from you, Daiko.

38:09.750 --> 38:11.310
It’s okay if we go together, isn’t it?

38:12.950 --> 38:14.810
Be really careful, will you?

38:15.430 --> 38:17.210
Shout if anything happens.

38:18.310 --> 38:20.060
I know.

38:23.470 --> 38:25.870
Not a hint of tension...

38:27.310 --> 38:28.280
Huh?

38:28.280 --> 38:29.890
What’s this?

38:30.740 --> 38:34.130
There must be a kitchen or something.

38:34.130 --> 38:35.680
R-Right.

38:39.130 --> 38:40.790
Don’t push yourself if you’re scared.

38:47.960 --> 38:49.340
Hey Ayu...

38:49.340 --> 38:50.550
Yes?

38:50.550 --> 38:54.260
What do you think of that Yoshinaga?

38:54.260 --> 38:55.480
What do I think?

38:55.480 --> 38:58.020
Sometimes his eyes are lewd.

38:58.020 --> 38:59.560
Really?

38:59.560 --> 39:01.400
I hate such eyes.

39:01.400 --> 39:03.610
EMAIL

39:01.400 --> 39:03.610
You've got mail
from Mr.Sosuke.

39:02.300 --> 39:03.610
Just like his...

39:04.380 --> 39:05.580
His?

39:06.550 --> 39:07.330
What?

39:07.330 --> 39:08.510
Sound of water!

39:09.930 --> 39:10.870
See?

39:10.870 --> 39:12.120
Where?

39:13.150 --> 39:14.690
Oh, again!

39:14.690 --> 39:16.040
Where?

39:16.040 --> 39:16.740
This way!

39:16.740 --> 39:17.330
Ayu!

39:22.760 --> 39:23.960
Ayu!

39:36.710 --> 39:37.800
Daiko...

39:38.790 --> 39:41.150
Where are you, Daiko?!

39:56.730 --> 39:58.520
It’s definitely this room.

39:58.520 --> 40:00.360
Ayu! Where are you?!

40:00.360 --> 40:03.770
Here! Come quick!

40:09.300 --> 40:12.170
This is that room from before!

40:26.650 --> 40:28.560
Ayu!

40:31.700 --> 40:34.140
I think it... moved just now...

40:35.140 --> 40:36.390
No, it couldn’t have.

40:38.280 --> 40:40.160
Ayu, where are you?!

40:40.570 --> 40:41.630
Ayu!

40:41.630 --> 40:42.540
What’s wrong?

40:42.540 --> 40:44.170
A-Ayu. Isn’t she back?

40:44.580 --> 40:46.040
No, what’s the matter?

40:46.710 --> 40:48.420
She disappeared suddenly.

40:48.420 --> 40:49.670
Disappeared?

40:50.300 --> 40:51.880
What happened?

40:51.880 --> 40:54.050
Somebody! Open this!

40:54.050 --> 40:55.680
Somebody!

40:56.040 --> 40:57.740
Daiko! Help!

40:57.740 --> 41:00.840
Daiko! Daiko! Daiko!

41:19.480 --> 41:21.120
Is... that... me?

41:32.440 --> 41:33.670
Teacher...

41:40.740 --> 41:43.480
You’re not moving your fingers correctly.

41:47.590 --> 41:51.110
I’ll give you more to work on next lesson.

41:51.110 --> 41:52.150
No...

41:52.910 --> 41:55.340
No more piano...

41:58.090 --> 41:59.410
Don’t...

42:00.210 --> 42:01.030
Don’t...

42:13.380 --> 42:14.460
Oh!

42:23.270 --> 42:24.880
Alright, Ayu-chan.

42:43.880 --> 42:44.910
I just...

42:45.970 --> 42:49.560
I just thought that
if the piano broke down...

42:50.140 --> 42:53.190
I wouldn’t have to practice...

42:54.540 --> 43:00.680
I never expected that to happen
to the teacher...

43:00.680 --> 43:02.410
It’s alright Ayu-chan,

43:03.200 --> 43:04.530
look at me.

43:14.120 --> 43:15.070
No...

43:16.060 --> 43:17.240
No more...

43:17.240 --> 43:18.570
Daiko...

43:19.530 --> 43:22.600
Help me... Daiko!

43:41.510 --> 43:43.720
KARUMA: MISERY SWIRLING DEMON

44:01.800 --> 44:09.740
In the darkness of night, laying in bed
Tonight also, ever deeper decadence

44:09.740 --> 44:19.540
Smeared with grotesque make-up
Heart and body soaked, so upside-down

44:21.150 --> 44:23.910
Upside-down

44:26.620 --> 44:34.790
Make you, make me thrilled
Under the moonlight, honey

44:34.790 --> 44:42.380
Spit upon the bound-up heart

44:42.380 --> 44:50.110
Do the trip
Come on let’s dance, mired in depravity

44:50.110 --> 44:59.260
In return for this degradation,
unhidden jealous heart

44:59.260 --> 45:03.380
Body lusting for riot

45:13.810 --> 45:15.810
Next Episode Preview

45:16.510 --> 45:19.230
Trapped in hopelessness with no escape...

45:19.230 --> 45:26.900
the houseguests are engulfed by
their own darkness, one by one.

45:27.840 --> 45:33.410
There was, however, a shadow of
an uninvited guest.

45:34.300 --> 45:38.830
Demon Prince Enma,
the final episode, “Enma.”

45:38.920 --> 45:38.960
ENMA

45:39.150 --> 45:42.830
Over there... something is lurking.
